# tools/cr/crypto_kumara_identity_witness.rish — the identity arc's FRONT DOOR authored in pure Rye, authoring NO new cryptography. The one
# composition that ties the whole arc into a single answer: from a backup phrase to a keeper's Kumara signing identity and the signature it makes.
# Where the rungs beneath authored each piece — crypto/bip39_seed folds a mnemonic to a 512-bit seed, crypto/slip10_ed25519 grows that seed into an
# ed25519 HD tree, crypto/kumara_path names the copyable shape m/44'/coin_type'/account'/index', crypto/ed25519_sign makes and derives the
# signature — this rung COMPOSES them so a caller reaches identity through one door: phrase → seed → path → keypair → signature. It is the
# identity-arc sibling of crypto/eth_address.rye and crypto/bitcoin_address.rye: where those render a key to its human address, this renders a
# phrase to the identity every Grain module signs and verifies with — Kumara, Vault, Comlink, the Lotus signed carry (crypto · Season G).
#
# Season: crypto — Season G (the Six-Season double-seat). This rung contributes only the wiring plus a two-way public-key check over already-GREEN
# rungs; every HMAC, clamp, scalar, and signature lives beneath, each proven byte-for-byte on metal. Design read:
# active-designing/date/20260815/20260815-175524_rye-first-crypto-parity-and-the-decision-wave.md (Season G · the crypto parity wave — the library that serves
# Kumara identity, Vault, Comlink, and the Lotus signed carry).
# Clean-room: the path convention, BIP-39, and SLIP-0010's vectors are public standards studied through their specs; no line is copied
# (.claude/rules/gratitude-licenses.md).
#
# Parity is proven at selftest three replayable ways, no fabricated constant: (1) the bip39 half is anchored to a REAL published answer — BIP-39's
# own Trezor vector mnemonic "abandon…about" under passphrase "TREZOR" folds to the spec's published 512-bit seed byte-for-byte; (2) the arc has no
# drift — from_mnemonic equals hand-wiring bip39_seed → kumara_path.derive_identity, from_seed reaches the identical identity, and the identity's
# public key equals both slip10's public form (0x00 tag stripped) and ed25519_sign's independent derive_public, all three agreeing (the ed25519 half
# proven one rung down against SLIP-0010's own ed25519 vectors); (3) the derived key is a REAL working signing key — it signs a message verify
# accepts, while a flipped message byte, a flipped signature byte, and a different identity's public key each refuse. Determinism and distinctness
# close the proof. Purely local — TEST identities from published vectors, no network, no funds; growing a real Kumara identity from the maintainer's
# own phrase and signing a real record with it stays the custody gate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/cr/crypto_kumara_identity_witness.rish

say "crypto-kumara-identity: Language EN — the identity arc's FRONT DOOR: the one composition that ties phrase → seed → path → keypair → signature into a single answer, the identity every Grain module signs and verifies with (Kumara, Vault, Comlink, the Lotus signed carry). The identity-arc sibling of crypto/eth_address and crypto/bitcoin_address: where those render a key to its human address, this renders a backup phrase to the Kumara signing identity. from_mnemonic folds a mnemonic to a 512-bit seed through the GREEN crypto/bip39_seed, walks crypto/kumara_path's m/44'/coin'/account'/index' over the GREEN crypto/slip10_ed25519 HD tree, and reads off the raw 32-byte ed25519 public key; sign / verify are thin wrappers over crypto/ed25519_sign + crypto/ed25519_verify. Authors NO new cryptography."
say "crypto-kumara-identity: Style Radiant — one backup phrase becomes a keeper's whole signing identity, reached the same way from the same phrase on any device, and every module that ever signs or verifies reaches it through one door. The wallet arc's render-to-address gesture turned toward Grain's own identity, authored in the open and proven against the standard's own answers."
say "crypto-kumara-identity: Lens TAME — every width named (a 32-byte secret seed, a 32-byte public key, a 32-byte chain code, u32 path slots), contract asserts on the walked node's depth, the SLIP-0010 domain tag, and the two independent public derivations agreeing byte-for-byte; it calls no cryptography of its own, only the GREEN rungs beneath. Parity holds three ways: the Trezor vector seed anchored byte-for-byte, the arc proven drift-free through hand-wiring, and the derived key proven a real working signing key by a sign/verify round-trip with three refusals. Purely local — TEST identities only, no real identity key, no network, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "crypto/bin/kumara_identity"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p crypto/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build crypto/kumara_identity.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "crypto-kumara-identity: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "crypto/bin/kumara_identity.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "crypto-kumara-identity: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "crypto-kumara-identity: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN crypto-kumara-identity' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "crypto-kumara-identity: selftest did not print the GREEN crypto-kumara-identity line"
